meta {
  name: Scenarios
  seq: 4
}

docs {
  # Service owner API scenarios

  BDD scenarios for the service owner endpoints under
  `/accessmanagement/api/v1/serviceowner`. They double as usage documentation: every
  request carries a `docs` block with what the endpoint does, the parameters it takes,
  the token and scope it needs, and the response it returns.

  Each subfolder is one scenario. The files inside are the scenario steps, named
  `NN_GIVEN|WHEN|THEN|AND|CLEANUP_...` and ordered by `seq`. A scenario starts from a
  known state, removes what it created, and can run standalone or repeatedly.

  ## Endpoints

  - `POST authorizedparties`: the parties a person or organization can act on behalf of,
    looked up by a service owner. Scope `altinn:accessmanagement/authorizedparties.resourceowner`.
  - `GET connections/resources/rights`, `POST connections/resources` and
    `POST connections/resources/revoke`: a service owner delegates single rights on its
    own resource from one party to another, and revokes them again. Scope
    `altinn:serviceowner/delegations:resource.write`, behind the feature flag
    `AccessMgmt.Controller.ServiceOwner.ResourceDelegation`.

  ## Tokens and fixtures

  Every step mints a Maskinporten enterprise token through `helpers.js`
  (`loginAsServiceOwner(serviceOwner, scope)`). The service owners come from
  `testdata/sharedtestdata.js`: digdir owns the delegated resource and skd does not. The
  resource and the two persons come from `testdata/serviceowner-scenarios/<env>.js`.

  ## Environments

  Written for and verified on AT22. In TT02 the API gateway answers 404 for
  serviceowner/authorizedparties and the three serviceowner/connections/resources endpoints,
  the same as for a path that does not exist (the rest of the service owner API, such as
  serviceowner/connections/accesspackages, works there). The folder skips every request where
  the environment lists serviceowner-authorizedparties-and-resources in notYetDeployed (see
  testdata/environment-features.js). Before removing it from TT02.bru, check the gateway route
  and the feature flag AccessMgmt.Controller.ServiceOwner.ResourceDelegation.
}

script:pre-request {
  const { FEATURES, notYetDeployed } = require("./testdata/environment-features.js");
  if (notYetDeployed(FEATURES.serviceOwnerAuthorizedPartiesAndResources)) {
    bru.runner.skipRequest();
  }
}
